{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPpg5aeyjaftVx2zMrMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a ROS2 (Robot Operating System 2) issue where:\n1. They have a subscriber to `/camera/image_raw` that never receives messages\n2. `ros2 topic hz /camera/image_raw` shows 30 Hz (so the topic is being published)\n3. The code compiles and the node starts without errors\n\nThis is a classic ROS2 subscription issue. The most common causes are:\n\n1. **Callback never being spun** - The most common issue. The node needs to be spun/executed for callbacks to be invoked. They might have created the subscription but not actually spinning the executor.\n\n2. **QoS mismatch** - The publisher and subscriber have incompatible Quality of Service settings. This is very common in ROS2.\n\n3. **Topic name mismatch** - Though they verify with `ros2 topic hz`, so this is unlikely.\n\n4. **Node not running** - But they say the node starts fine.\n\n5. **Callback not defined properly** - Though they say it compiles.\n\nSince this is a diagnostic question about their code (which I don't see), I should ask clarifying questions to help them identify the issue. However, the most common causes are:\n\n- **QoS mismatch** - ROS2 uses transient_local vs volatile QoS by default, and camera images typically use volatile. If their subscriber uses a different QoS than the publisher, they won't connect.\n- **Not spinning the executor** - If they're not calling `executor.spin()` or similar, the callbacks won't be called.\n\nI should ask to see their code or guide them through the most likely causes. Since I don't have their code, I'll provide the most common causes and how to diagnose/fix them.\n\nLet me provide a concise diagnosis of the most likely issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6554,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6554},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ea3e478-f8c5-4323-b61f-6b387e981603","uuid":"6c51cd5c-4267-4f86-afbf-c126a1cf06a7","timestamp":"2026-07-26T01:44:50.384Z","request_id":"req_011CdPpg4dbo1zUoK77YnRQa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPpg5aeyjaftVx2zMrMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is almost always a **QoS (Quality of Service) mismatch** or **not spinning the executor**. Here are the most common causes:\n\n**1. QoS mismatch (most common)**\nCamera publishers typically use `SENSOR_DATA` QoS (volatile, best-effort). If your subscriber uses the default `DEFAULT` QoS (transient_local, reliable), they won't connect.\n\n```cpp\n// Subscribe with matching QoS\nauto qos_profile = rclcpp::SensorDataQoS();  // or rclcpp::QoS(10).best_effort()\nsubscription_ = node_->create_subscription<sensor_msgs::msg::Image>(\n    \"/camera/image_raw\", \n    qos_profile,  // Add this!\n    [this](const sensor_msgs::msg::Image::SharedPtr msg) { /* ... */ });\n```\n\nCheck what the publisher uses: `ros2 topic info /camera/image_raw -v` and match it.\n\n**2. Not spinning the executor**\nYour callback won't fire unless you spin:\n\n```cpp\nrclcpp::spin(node_);  // Required! This runs the event loop\n```\n\nOr if using an executor:\n```cpp\nrclcpp::executors::SingleThreadedExecutor executor;\nexecutor.add_node(node_);\nexecutor.spin();  // This invokes callbacks\n```\n\n**3. Quick diagnostics**\n- Post your subscriber code (especially QoS settings and the spin call)\n- Run: `ros2 topic info /camera/image_raw -v` to see publisher QoS\n- Check if your node is actually blocking on `spin()` or exits immediately\n\nWhich of these sounds most likely?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6554,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6554},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ea3e478-f8c5-4323-b61f-6b387e981603","uuid":"013b6120-9a82